    {
      "id": "p3",
      "text": "The decision that initiated the dispute, announced by the production's decision-maker, drew hostile online reactions and a public accusation from commentators. Yet those who advocated for shared heritage countered with a cultural perspective, arguing for an inclusive interpretation of the Western canon. This social conflict turned the adaptation into a flashpoint over identity, with the resulting public debate centering on belonging and cultural ownership in film.",
